     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Bases",
     "md": "**Binary** is base 2 (0, 1). **Octal** is base 8 (0 to 7). **Denary** is base 10. **Hexadecimal** (hex) is base 16: 0 to 9 and A to F (A = 10 ... F = 15). Computers use binary; hex and octal are shorter ways to write binary."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "Denary to binary",
