    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "Binary and hex",
     "md": "Group the bits in **fours** from the right. 1010 0111 = A7 (1010 = A, 0111 = 7). Denary value of A7 = 10 x 16 + 7 = 167. For octal, group bits in threes."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Mistakes",
     "md": "- Group from the **right**.\n- Hex letters stand for 10-15.\n- Hex is used because it is shorter for humans, not because computers use it."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 1",
     "statement": "Convert 100 to binary.",
     "steps": [
      "100 = 64 + 32 + 4.",
      "Bits 128..1 are 0 1 1 0 0 1 0 0."
     ],
     "answer": "01100100"
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 2",
     "statement": "Convert 10100111 to hex and denary.",
     "steps": [
      "1010 0111 = A 7, so hex A7.",
      "Denary: 10 x 16 + 7 = 167."
     ],
     "answer": "A7 = 167"
    }
