        "color": "ink"
       }
      ]
     },
     "caption": "Column sum of 101 and 011 giving 1000.",
     "alt": "Binary addition: 101 + 011 = 1000, that is 5 + 3 = 8."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "Overflow",
     "md": "If an answer needs more bits than a store can hold, **overflow** occurs. In 8 bits the largest unsigned number is 255 (11111111)."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Mistakes",
     "md": "- Forgetting a carry.\n- Not checking the answer by converting to denary.\n- Ignoring overflow in a fixed number of bits."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 1",
     "statement": "Add 101 and 011.",
     "steps": [
      "Right column: 1+1 = 10, write 0 carry 1. Middle: 0+1+1 = 10, write 0 carry 1.",
      "Left: 1+0+1 = 10, write 0 carry 1, so the answer is 1000. Check: 5+3 = 8."
     ],
     "answer": "1000"
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 2",
     "statement": "Shift 00000110 left by two places.",
     "steps": [
      "6 shifted left once is 12 (00001100).",
      "Shifted twice: 24 (00011000)."
     ],
     "answer": "24"
    }
   ],
