   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Characters",
     "md": "Text is stored as codes. **ASCII** gives every character a number: A = 65, a = 97, 0 = 48. Standard ASCII has 128 codes (7 bits). **Unicode** has many more so it can store letters of many languages."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "Images",
     "md": "A **bitmap** image is a grid of **pixels**. **Resolution** = pixels across x pixels down. **Colour depth** = bits per pixel. File size (bits) = width x height x colour depth; divide by 8 for bytes."
    },
